#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid "Style"
msgstr "Estil"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This module is used to configure how the individual widgets are drawn by "
"&kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <emphasis>Widget</emphasis> is a commonly-used programmer's term for "
"referring to User Interface elements such as buttons, menus, and scroll "
"bars. You can think of them as the fundamental pieces that are assembled to "
"make your application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can configure how the widgets are drawn with this module, but to change "
"the color of the widgets, you should refer to the section entitled <ulink "
"url=\"help:/kcontrol/color/index.html\">Colors</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This panel is divided into three tabs: <guilabel>Style</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Effects</guilabel>, <guilabel>Toolbar</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Style</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top list box, labeled <guilabel>Widget Style</guilabel> contains a list "
"of the pre-defined styles. Each style has a name, and a brief description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change styles, simply click on the style name, and a preview of the style "
"will be displayed in the preview box below the style list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "The other options available here are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show icons on buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, action buttons (like <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"and <guibutton>Apply</guibutton>) will have a small icon located within them "
"to act as a visual reference. If this option is not selected, then only text "
"will appear on the button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable tooltips"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will toggle tooltips off and on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Effects</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you click on the <guilabel>Effects</guilabel> tab, you will see the panel "
"is divided into two sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the top of the first section, is a checkbox labeled <guilabel>Enable GUI "
"effects</guilabel>. If there is no mark in front of this checkbox, then all "
"visual effects of this panel are disabled. To edit any of these effects, "
"simply place a mark in this checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Below that checkbox, are the following choices:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "Combobox effect:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This combobox has two options. If this option is set to <guilabel>Animate</"
"guilabel> then when a combo box is selected, it will appear to scroll down. "
"If <guilabel>Disable</guilabel> is selected, then the combobox list appears "
"instantly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tool tip effect:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This combobox has three options. If this option is set to <guilabel>Animate</"
"guilabel> then when a tool tip appears, it will have a short animation. If "
"<guilabel>Fade</guilabel> is selected, the tool tip appears to fade from the "
"background. If <guilabel>Disable</guilabel> is selected, then the tool tip "
"appears instantly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu effect:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This combobox has four options. If this option is set to <guilabel>Animate</"
"guilabel> then when a menu list appears, it will appear to scroll downward. "
"If <guilabel>Fade</guilabel> is selected, the menu list appears to fade from "
"the background. If <guilabel>Make Transparent</guilabel> is selected, the "
"menu list will have a transparent look to it. The details of that "
"transparency is configured in the next part of the dialog. If "
"<guilabel>Disable</guilabel> is selected, then the menu list appears "
"instantly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu tear-off handles:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is set to <guilabel>Disable</guilabel>, then no menus can be "
"separated from the application. If <guilabel>Application Level</guilabel> is "
"selected, then it is left up to each individual application to determine "
"which menus can be torn separated from the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many applications do not have tear off menus. You cannot tell &kde; to force "
"an application to allow tear off menus. This is determined by the authors of "
"the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next checkbox, labeled <guilabel>Menu drop shadow</guilabel> is used to "
"toggle the drop shadow behind all &kde; menus. A drop shadow is a dark, soft "
"line on the bottom and right sides of the menu, which give the menus the "
"appearance that the menu is lifted off the application, and the menu is "
"creating a shadow on the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next section only applies if the combobox labeled <guilabel>Menu Effect</"
"guilabel> is set to <guilabel>Make Transparent</guilabel>. You can use the "
"combo box labeled <guilabel>Menu transparency type:</guilabel> to select the "
"method &kde; uses to generate the transparency. You can use the slider to "
"determine the level of transparency in menus. A preview is visible on the "
"right side of this section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Toolbar</guilabel> tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight buttons under mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is a mark in this checkbox, when the mouse pointer is above a "
"toolbar button, that button will be highlighted with a square around the "
"button. This is a good visual indicator of which button will be selected "
"with a mouse click."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Transparent toolbars when moving"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As the title suggests, if this option is selected, the toolbars will be "
"transparent when you are moving them around on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This combo box lets you determine where on the button the text name of the "
"button will appear as the default. If <guilabel>Icon Only</guilabel> is "
"selected, then there is no text on the toolbar buttons. If <guilabel>Text "
"Only</guilabel> is selected, then the button's icon is replaced with a text "
"name of the button. If <guilabel>Text Alongside Icons</guilabel> is "
"selected, then the name of the button will be placed to the <emphasis>right</"
"emphasis> of the icon. If <guilabel>Text Under Icons</guilabel> is selected, "
"the default will be to have the text of the button <emphasis>below</"
"emphasis> the icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option only specifies the <emphasis>default</emphasis> location. Each "
"application can override the setting used in this panel."
msgstr ""

